1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,970
They prepaid this hotel room.

2
00:00:01,970 --> 00:00:03,227
The front desk said:

3
00:00:03,227 --> 00:00:04,646
"We're sold out."

4
00:00:04,646 --> 00:00:05,640
That same night,

5
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:06,642
their new room cost

6
00:00:06,642 --> 00:00:08,407
$1,400.

7
00:00:08,487 --> 00:00:09,965
Nassau, the Bahamas.

8
00:00:09,965 --> 00:00:11,535
Kristine and Jimmy Dworkin,

9
00:00:11,535 --> 00:00:12,812
from California.

10
00:00:12,812 --> 00:00:14,624
Night one of an 8-day trip:

11
00:00:14,624 --> 00:00:17,029
a Courtyard by Marriott. Prepaid.

12
00:00:17,029 --> 00:00:18,741
At check-in… no room.

13
00:00:18,741 --> 00:00:20,465
The hotel was overbooked.

14
00:00:20,465 --> 00:00:21,935
Kristine says the staff were

15
00:00:21,935 --> 00:00:23,729
"pretty rude about it."

16
00:00:23,759 --> 00:00:25,700
Hotels often overbook on purpose:

17
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:27,478
some guests never show up.

18
00:00:27,508 --> 00:00:28,664
So around midnight,

19
00:00:28,664 --> 00:00:30,835
they walked the streets of Nassau.

20
00:00:30,835 --> 00:00:31,787
One room left:

21
00:00:31,787 --> 00:00:33,515
a suite at Margaritaville.

22
00:00:33,515 --> 00:00:35,131
$1,400.

23
00:00:35,131 --> 00:00:36,299
For 1 night.

24
00:00:36,429 --> 00:00:38,408
They started emailing for help.

25
00:00:38,408 --> 00:00:41,062
Kristine says Marriott did… nothing.

26
00:00:41,092 --> 00:00:43,100
So they contacted NBC Bay Area.

27
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:44,590
A hospitality professor told

28
00:00:44,590 --> 00:00:45,952
NBC big hotels usually pay

29
00:00:45,952 --> 00:00:47,981
for your first night elsewhere.

30
00:00:47,981 --> 00:00:49,847
Marriott's website, NBC found,

31
00:00:49,847 --> 00:00:51,488
only promises a new room…

32
00:00:51,488 --> 00:00:52,819
to elite members.

33
00:00:52,849 --> 00:00:55,020
Then Marriott agreed to pay them back:

34
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:56,285
the $1,400,

35
00:00:56,285 --> 00:00:57,921
plus the original room.

36
00:00:58,001 --> 00:00:59,638
In hotel slang, being sent to

37
00:00:59,638 --> 00:01:02,347
another hotel is called getting "walked."

38
00:01:02,347 --> 00:01:04,685
Usually, the hotel arranges the walk.

39
00:01:04,685 --> 00:01:06,656
This time, the family did it…

40
00:01:06,656 --> 00:01:08,800
on foot.
